        "committer": {
          "name": "Patrick Farrell",
          "email": "patrick@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-12 16:23:24.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-20076 tests: time remote commands on CI nodes",
        "message": "LU-20076 tests: time remote commands on CI nodes\n\nNot for landing.  Console markers from Maloo runs show a remote\ncommand costs about 0.55 s on CI nodes, and about 0.35 s with ssh\nconnection sharing (69318), while the same do_node takes about\n0.04 s with sharing on a VM test cluster.  A command the driver\nruns locally also takes about 0.2 s in CI.  conf-sanity runs\nover 40000 remote commands, so this cost is most of its run time.\n\nAdd sanity test_999p, which times the parts of a remote command\non the nodes it runs on: local fork and bash startup, lctl mark,\ndo_node with and without VERBOSE, new and shared ssh connections,\npdsh, and fork and bash startup on each server.  It also prints\nthe ssh, sshd and load settings that bear on the result.  Every\nline it prints starts with TIMING_PROBE.\n\nTest-Parameters: fortestonly testlist=sanity env=ONLY=999p mdscount=2 mdtcount=4\nTest-Parameters: fortestonly testlist=sanity env=ONLY=999p fstype=zfs mdscount=2 mdtcount=4\nTest-Parameters: fortestonly testlist=sanity env=ONLY=999p\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Id007610a5b92bec4b1c754d7389cd72f944a72bf\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
